  "body": "**Stacked on #964** (issue #906, branch `issue/906-c-unwind-rate-cap`). This PR is based on `main` because GitHub cannot base a cross-repo PR on a fork branch, so until #964 merges its diff also shows #964's two commits (`b21879ac`, `d1e1245a`). This PR's own commit is the last one; review it alone with its commit view. Merge #964 first.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` (`liveMove`): #964 refused a C-turning rapid in a C section when the machine states a C travel but no C rate. This PR drops the travel condition. A C-turning rapid on a machine that states **no C rate** is now refused by name whether a C travel is stated or not. The text names what is missing: \"a C-axis rapid that turns C, but the machine file states no C rate - its feed would be uncapped; state the C axis's speeds\". When a travel is stated it still reads \"a C travel but no C rate\", so #964's pinned text holds. Cut moves are unchanged, because their F is the planned feed along the part-frame chord.\n- `crates/app/tests/c_axis_live.rs`: the `c_axis_live` bench (a test fixture, not a builder's data) now states a C rate: feed 6000 and rapid 12000 deg/min, the same figures as the shipped `millturn.mch`. Before this, its contour test posted C-turning link rapids on that bench at exactly the uncapped F this issue is about. The new test covers the no-rate case on an `unrated` copy of the same bench.\n- `docs/decisions/966-lathe-c-no-rate.md`: why I chose a refusal over a no-F form (G00 with C follows no verified path; a G01 without F inherits an unrelated modal feed), why there is no generation gate, and why the bench changed.\n\n## Readings\n\nOn the old bench (no C travel, no C rate), `a_rotary_contour_on_the_spindle_states_c_on_every_move_and_posts` posted its C-turning link rapids with no cap. With the fix and the old bench, that test fails with the new refusal, which confirms that the bench's contour did reach the uncapped branch. With the bench stating 6000 deg/min, every X Z C G01 of that program reads back inside 4000 mm/min linear and 6000 deg/min C.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `c_axis_live::a_c_turning_rapid_without_a_stated_c_rate_is_refused_by_name` generates the bench's Rotary Contour and checks that it really does link by C-turning rapids. Posted through `fanuc-lathe.cps` on the bench with no C travel and no C rate, it is refused by name. On the rated bench it posts clean, and every F is checked against the stated linear and C rates.\n- #964's `c_axis_unwind::the_lathe_post_refuses_a_c_turning_rapid_without_a_stated_c_rate` and `rotary_gate::a_rewind_without_a_stated_c_rate_is_refused_by_name` still pass unchanged.\n\n## Moved goldens\n\nNone. `tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/c_axis_helix.nc` is unchanged: its rapids turn no C, and its cuts run well under 6000 deg/min. `c_axis_unwind`'s two-rings golden is unchanged too.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 1.8 min (app lib + `c_axis_fixture`, `c_axis_live`, `c_axis_unwind`); `cargo xtask gate test a_c_turning_rapid_without_a_stated_c_rate_is_refused_by_name --crate camcraft-app --binary c_axis_live` green; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test c_axis_live -- -D warnings` clean\n- Extra suites: `lathe_post` 7, `lathe_post_refusals` 6, `lathe_post_g76` 8, `lathe_spindle_law` 8, `posting` 17, `golden_cl` 25, `conformance` 6, `program_entry` 9, `coolant_followups` 7 - all pass\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI and MCP paths. They post through the same engine and `.cps`, and no command or MCP surface changed.\n- The release-tier heavy lanes.\n- Other lathe posts (`tormach-lathe` and the rest) do not declare `liveTooling`. The engine refuses C sections for them, so they cannot reach this case.\n\nChangelog: The Fanuc lathe post refuses by name a C-axis rapid that turns C on a machine that states no C rate, whether or not it states a C travel, instead of posting it at an uncapped feed (#966)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #966\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
